---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Technology Overview | AC-130 Viper" description="Explore the AC-130 Viper localized CO₂ cooling platform and its engineering development.">
  <main>
    <section class="sub-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / TECHNOLOGY</p>
        <h1>Technology, designed with purpose.</h1>
        <p>Explore the system components and engineering program behind the AC-130 Viper. The final design and capabilities are not yet established.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section"><div class="container split-layout">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">DEVELOPMENT PLATFORM</p><h2>Localized CO₂ cooling technology</h2><p>The AC-130 Viper is a localized CO₂ cooling device being developed by New York Cryogen, Inc. Work includes the handheld applicator, control interface, cooling-delivery configuration and supporting system integration.</p><p>Any photographs show development-related equipment and should not be interpreted as final commercial specifications.</p></div>
      <figure class="content-image"><img src="/images/viper-device.png" alt="AC-130 Viper development monitor and handheld applicator" width="1000" height="562" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Product-development imagery; configuration may change.</figcaption></figure>
    </div></section>
    <section class="content-section light-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">ENGINEERING AREAS</p><h2>Technology under development</h2><div class="info-grid">
      <article class="info-card"><h3>Applicator design</h3><p>Continued refinement of the handheld assembly and mechanical design.</p></article>
      <article class="info-card"><h3>Cooling delivery</h3><p>Engineering work focused on localized CO₂ delivery system configuration.</p></article>
      <article class="info-card"><h3>Monitoring interface</h3><p>Development of display and monitoring components; features are not final.</p></article>
    </div></div></section>
    <section class="content-section"><div class="container split-layout reverse"><figure class="content-image"><img src="/images/ny-cryogen-studio.jpg" alt="New York Cryogen workspace and technology development equipment" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy"/></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">IMPORTANT INFORMATION</p><h2>Specifications remain subject to review</h2><p>The website does not establish final settings, operating parameters, clinical performance, indications, contraindications, or safety claims. Such information will depend on final product development and applicable regulatory review.</p><a class="text-link" href="/research-development/">Read about development ↗</a></div></div></section>

    <section class="sub-cta">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">STAY CONNECTED</p>
        <h2>Follow the development of AC-130 Viper.</h2>
        <p>For product-development, company, business or media inquiries, contact New York Cryogen.</p>
        <a class="button-primary" href="/contact/">Contact New York Cryogen ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
